hi everyone and welcome to biology  professor today we're going to learn  about an important math skill that comes  up in biology and other types of science  and that is identifying place values  what this means is that in any kind of  measurement situation where you have a  number for example here we're using 1234  point 5 6 7 these different digits  within the number hold different place  values for example here the one is at  the thousands place the two is in the  hundreds place the three is in tens  place the 4 is in the ones place then  you have the decimal point the 5 is in  the tenths place  note the THS the 6 is in the hundredths  place which also has the THS on the end  and the seven is in the thousandths  place  again with that THS that distinguishes  these three from these top three now  identifying place values when is this  important well it's important whenever  you're using the metric system so when  you are converting between different  prefixes whenever you're doing any kind  of rounding also working with scientific  notation moving numbers from standard  notation like you see here into  scientific notation and also when using  significant figures which plays a  heavier role in chemistry but does have  some applications and biology as well so  that is it for identifying place values  I hope you learned a lot and we'll see  you next time
 

